    "created_at": "2017-01-03T09:25:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-03T09:25:06Z",
    "body": "Sounds like a fascinating project!\r\n\r\nEven if we were to annotate all the event handler attributes with the event interface that's used for that event type, it would still be possible for scripts to create events of the same type but a different interface and dispatch on the same object. Would that be a problem?\r\n\r\nAlso note that some event types are used by multiple interfaces, for example \"error\", where an Event is used for HTMLImageElement, but an ErrorEvent is used in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#runtime-script-errors (*target* is the global object in at least one call site)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
