    "created_at": "2017-01-03T10:32:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-03T12:47:37Z",
    "body": ">it would still be possible for scripts to create events of the same type but a different interface and dispatch on the same object\r\n\r\nI don't think that will be a problem. I only need event interfaces for browser-dispatched *trusted* events to provide *default* argument type for event listeners. Users with manual dispatching will still be able to manually annotate their own expected event interface.\r\n\r\n>Also note that some event types are used by multiple interfaces\r\n\r\nTypeScript currently uses a 'event map' to match them:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ninterface HTMLBodyElementEventMap extends HTMLElementEventMap {\r\n    \"afterprint\": Event;\r\n    \"beforeprint\": Event;\r\n    \"beforeunload\": BeforeUnloadEvent;\r\n    \"blur\": FocusEvent;\r\n    \"error\": ErrorEvent;\r\n    \"focus\": FocusEvent;\r\n    \"hashchange\": HashChangeEvent;\r\n    \"load\": Event;\r\n    \"message\": MessageEvent;\r\n    \"offline\": Event;\r\n    \"online\": Event;\r\n    \"orientationchange\": Event;\r\n    \"pagehide\": PageTransitionEvent;\r\n    \"pageshow\": PageTransitionEvent;\r\n    \"popstate\": PopStateEvent;\r\n    \"resize\": UIEvent;\r\n    \"storage\": StorageEvent;\r\n    \"unload\": Event;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt will be great to see the spec provide similar one for each HTML interfaces in WebIDL.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/270086760/reactions",
